40. {#span-toggle-root; open} Span toggle fixture root
  1. {#span-toggle-node} Toggle [first]{=> #st-alpha} and [second]{=> #st-beta} here
  2. {#span-toggle-auto-node} Auto [alpha]{option; => #st-alpha} and [beta]{option; => #st-beta} here
  3. {#span-toggle-mixed-node} Mixed [opt]{option; => #st-alpha} and [tog]{=> #st-beta} here
  4. {#span-toggle-listbox-node; listbox} Listbox [one]{=> #st-alpha} and [two]{=> #st-beta} here
  5. {#span-toggle-hill-node} Hill [opt]{option; => #st-alpha} and [tog]{=> #st-beta} here
  6. {#span-toggle-block-node; = block}
      ~~~
      Block prose with a [toggle]{=> #st-alpha} span in it.
      ~~~
  7. {#span-toggle-math-block; = block}
      ~~~
      Math $x^2$ forces a re-render, and a [*styled*]{=> #st-beta} span survives it.
      ~~~
  8. {#span-toggle-euclid-node} Euclid [cite]{=> #st-alpha} then ([de]{selected; option; let &st-lang = de} / [en]{option; let &st-lang = en})
  9. {#span-toggle-langblock-node; = block}
      ~~~
      Cite a [source]{=> #st-alpha} then switch ([de]{selected; option; let &st-lang = de} / [en]{option; let &st-lang = en}).
      [Deutscher Text]{show-when: &st-lang == de}[English text]{show-when: &st-lang == en}
      ~~~
  15. {#span-toggle-whole-node} Whole [cite]{=> ^#st-alpha} beside children [tog]{=> #st-beta} here
  16. {#span-toggle-whole-leaf-node} Leaf cite [post]{=> ^#st-leaf} here
  10. {#span-toggle-langblock-peer; = block}
      ~~~
      A peer block writing the SAME variable ([la]{selected; option; let &st-lang = la} / [nl]{option; let &st-lang = nl} / [en]{option; let &st-lang = en}).
      [Latine]{show-when: &st-lang == la}[Nederlands]{show-when: &st-lang == nl}
      ~~~
  11. {#span-toggle-wrapped-node; = block}
      ~~~
      A citation [*puer aeternus*,]{=> #st-alpha} in prose that
      continues across lines before the switch.
      ([de]{selected; option; let &st-w = de} / [en]{option; let &st-w = en})

      > [Der Mensch, insofern er wirklich sein will, muß dasein,
      und zu dem Ende muß er sich begrenzen.
      Wer gegen das Endliche zu ekel ist, der kommt zu gar keiner Wirklichkeit,
      sondern er verbleibt im Abstrakten.]{show-when: &st-w == de}
      [Man, insofar as he wants to be actual, must be determinate,
      and to that end must limit himself.
      Whoever loathes the finite too much, he attains no actuality at all,
      but remains in the abstract.]{show-when: &st-w == en}
      ~~~
  12. {#span-toggle-nonempty-node; = block; listbox-nonempty}
      ~~~
      A citation [source]{=> #st-alpha} beside a switch that can never be
      cleared ([la]{selected; option; let &st-ne = la} / [en]{option; let &st-ne = en}).
      [Latine]{show-when: &st-ne == la}[English]{show-when: &st-ne == en}
      ~~~
  14. {#span-toggle-tall-block; = block}
      ~~~
      A body taller than the scroller's 30vh cap. Line two.
      Line three. Line four. Line five. Line six. Line seven. Line eight.
      Line nine. Line ten. Line eleven. Line twelve. Line thirteen.
      Line fourteen. Line fifteen. Line sixteen. Line seventeen.
      Line eighteen. Line nineteen. Line twenty. Line twenty-one.
      Line twenty-two. Line twenty-three. Line twenty-four.
      Line twenty-five. Line twenty-six. Line twenty-seven.
      Line twenty-eight. Line twenty-nine. Line thirty. Line thirty-one.
      Line thirty-two. Line thirty-three. Line thirty-four.
      Line thirty-five. Line thirty-six. Line thirty-seven.
      Line thirty-eight. Line thirty-nine. Line forty.
      ~~~
  13. {#span-toggle-nonempty-implicit; = block; listbox-nonempty}
      ~~~
      No option marked selected ([one]{option; let &st-ni = one} / [two]{option; let &st-ni = two}).
      [First]{show-when: &st-ni == one}[Second]{show-when: &st-ni == two}
      ~~~
